<!-- This vignette is precomputed, because it needs the model executable.
     Edit R3DFEM.Rmd.orig and run vignettes/precompute.R to update R3DFEM.Rmd -->

```{r setup, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(collapse = TRUE, comment = "#>", fig.width = 7, fig.height = 4,
                      fig.path = "figures/", dpi = 96, message = FALSE)
```

R3DFEM is an R interface to the version 5.7 of the
[3D-CMCC-FEM](https://www.forest-modelling-lab.com/the-3d-cmcc-model), a
bio-geochemical, process-based forest model that simulates carbon, water and nitrogen
fluxes and stocks of homogeneous and heterogeneous forests. This vignette shows the
whole workflow: install the model, prepare the inputs, run one or many simulations, read
and plot the outputs. The creation of the input files is described in detail in
`vignette("input-files")`.

```{r load}
library(R3DFEM)
```

## Installing the model

The package does not contain the model executable. `install_model()` downloads the
Windows build of the version 5.7 once, in a user directory; an executable already on
disk can be installed with `install_model("path/to/3D_CMCC_Forest_Model_5.7.exe")` or
used directly with `options(R3DFEM.exe = "path/to/executable")` (e.g. a binary compiled
on Linux from the [source code](https://github.com/Forest-Modelling-Lab/3D-CMCC-FEM)).

```{r install, eval = FALSE}
install_model()
```

```{r model}
model_available()
```

## Inputs

A simulation needs a directory with the stand, meteo, CO2, soil and topography files
of the site and the parameterization of the species. The package contains complete
input sets for three sites and the parameterizations of the version 5.7 for
`r length(list_species())` species:

```{r data}
bk <- system.file("extdata", "bilykriz", "rcp0p0", package = "R3DFEM")
list.files(bk)
list_species()
```

`setup_inputs()` prepares an input directory in one call, from files, values or
arguments of the `make_*()` helpers, and copies the species files. Here we start a new
site from the Bily Kriz weather, with a stand of two cohorts of Norway spruce:

```{r setup-inputs}
inputdir <- file.path(tempdir(), "spruce")
files <- setup_inputs("Spruce", inputdir,
                      stand = list(year = 1997, age = c(16, 30), species = "Piceaabies",
                                   n_trees = c(2000, 300), avdbh = c(7.1, 18), height = c(5.6, 14)),
                      soil = list(lat = 49.3, lon = 18.32, clay = 20.6, silt = 20.6,
                                  sand = 58.8, soil_depth = 80),
                      topo = 875,
                      meteo = file.path(bk, "BilyKriz_meteo.txt"),
                      co2 = file.path(bk, "BilyKriz_co2.txt"),
                      management = list(thinning = c(2005, 2015), thinning_int = c(20, 20),
                                        harvesting = 2025))
basename(files)
```

`check_inputs()` performs the checks of `run_3DCMCCFEM()` without running the model, for
example the harvest of 2025 requires the replanting arguments:

```{r check, error = TRUE}
check_inputs("Spruce", "Piceaabies", year_start = 1997, year_end = 2040,
             man = "var", pres_dens = "off", inputdir = inputdir)
```

## Running the model

`run_3DCMCCFEM()` writes the settings file in `inputdir`, runs the model and returns the
paths of the outputs, named by type. The model cannot write files whose full path is
longer than 260 characters: use short output directories.

```{r run}
out <- "C:/r3dfem_vignette"

off <- run_3DCMCCFEM(site = "Spruce", species = "Piceaabies",
                     year_start = 1997, year_end = 2040, man = "off",
                     output = "annual", inputdir = inputdir,
                     outputdir = file.path(out, "off"))

var <- run_3DCMCCFEM(site = "Spruce", species = "Piceaabies",
                     year_start = 1997, year_end = 2040,
                     man = "var", pres_dens = "off",
                     rep_species = "Piceaabies", rep_trees = 2000, rep_age = 3,
                     rep_dbh = 1, rep_lai = 1, rep_height = 1.3,
                     output = "annual", inputdir = inputdir,
                     outputdir = file.path(out, "var"))
basename(var)
```

`read_output()` reads an output as a data.frame (one row per year, layer and class):

```{r read}
a <- read_output(var[["annual"]])
a[a$YEAR %in% c(2004:2006, 2024:2026), c("YEAR", "LAYER", "AGE", "LIVETREE", "DBH", "HEIGHT", "NPP")]
```

## Plotting

`plot_output_3DFEM()` plots one or more variables (optionally with a rolling mean) or a
variable against another:

```{r plot-output, fig.height = 5}
plot_output_3DFEM(var[["annual"]], y = c("GPP", "NPP", "LIVETREE", "DBH"), text_size = 14)
```

## Many simulations

`run_batch()` runs a set of simulations, one per row of a data.frame, each in its own
directory with a copy of the inputs. The columns are arguments of `run_3DCMCCFEM()` (or
parameters of the species file, see below); `inputdir` can change from run to run. With
`parallel = TRUE` the simulations are run with the future plan set by the user:

```{r batch}
sites <- system.file("extdata", c("bilykriz/rcp0p0", "hyytiala", "soro"), package = "R3DFEM")
runs <- data.frame(id = c("bilykriz", "hyytiala", "soroe"),
                   site = c("BilyKriz", "Hyytiala", "Soroe"),
                   species = c("Piceaabies", "Pinussylvestris", "Fagussylvatica"),
                   inputdir = sites)

future::plan("multisession", workers = 3)
res <- run_batch(runs, outputdir = file.path(out, "sites"), year_start = 1997,
                 year_end = 2050, man = "off", output = "annual", parallel = TRUE)
future::plan("sequential")
res[, c("id", "status")]
```

The outputs of all the runs can be read together:

```{r batch-plot}
all <- read_output(res$output)
all$site <- basename(dirname(dirname(all$file)))
ggplot2::ggplot(all, ggplot2::aes(YEAR, NPP, colour = site)) +
  ggplot2::geom_line() +
  ggplot2::theme_classic()
```

Columns named as species parameters change the parameterization of each run.
`param_sensitivity()` uses this to show the effect of a parameter:

```{r sensitivity}
s <- param_sensitivity("LIGHT_TOL", value = 1:4, variable = c("GPP", "HEIGHT"),
                       inputdir = bk, outputdir = file.path(out, "sens"),
                       site = "BilyKriz", species = "Piceaabies",
                       year_start = 1997, year_end = 2050, man = "off")
s$plot
```

## Virtual stands

`virtual_stand_generator()` simulates the stand development and writes stand files for
age classes that are not observed, to be used as starting points of new simulations:

```{r virtual}
vdir <- file.path(tempdir(), "bk")
dir.create(vdir)
invisible(file.copy(list.files(bk, full.names = TRUE), vdir))
vs <- virtual_stand_generator(site = "BilyKriz", species = "Piceaabies", stand_age = c(40, 60),
                              man = "off", inputdir = vdir, outputdir = file.path(out, "virtual"))
vs[, c("Age", "Species", "N", "AvDBH", "Height")]
```

```{r cleanup, include = FALSE}
unlink(out, recursive = TRUE)
```

## References

R3DFEM: an R package for running the 3D-CMCC-FEM model.
*Earth Science Informatics* (2025). <https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12145-025-01956-0>

The model User Guide, with the full description of inputs and outputs, is available on
the [Forest Modelling Lab web page](https://www.forest-modelling-lab.com/the-3d-cmcc-model).
